+R2,audit behavior,"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 returns a dict only; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 creates no audit table","No durable audit trail exists for create or read operations despite documentation implying one","Persist audit events through a repository/table or emit them to an external durable sink","Backend owner or compliance-focused engineer"
+R3,configuration/runtime environment,"minisvc/config.py:10-13 parses MINISVC_READONLY, but minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 and minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 never enforce it","Runtime safety flags can be assumed active while writes still occur","Thread readonly configuration into the request path or repository and reject writes when enabled","Service owner"
+R4,API input validation,"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(...); no validation or exception handling is present","Malformed requests can raise uncaught exceptions or create inconsistent API behavior","Validate payload shape and types before model construction and convert failures into explicit client errors","API owner"
+R5,HTTP bootstrap coupling,"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes caller-provided app and repo; minisvc/cli.py:7-12 initializes schema separately and does not assemble the HTTP runtime","An embedding app can register routes without initializing schema or consistent config","Provide a single application factory that loads config, initializes storage, and registers routes together","Platform or integration owner"
+R6,error handling/retry,"minisvc/api/handlers.py:12 calls repo.save(order) once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 exposes sqlite errors directly","Transient database errors and duplicate key failures bubble up without controlled responses or retries","Define error mapping and retry policy at handler or service boundary","Backend owner"
